//
// Park 5-species air, 17 reversible reactions.
//
// Backward rates are NOT tabulated. neReversibleReaction evaluates
//     k_b(T) = k_f(T) / Keq(T)
// at runtime, in log space, with T = TTR (never the Park rate-controlling
// temperature). This makes forward and backward rates thermodynamically
// consistent by construction.
//
// Keq curve fit
// -------------
//     ln Keq = A1 + A2*Z + A3*Z^2 + A4*Z^3 + A5*Z^4,   Z = 10000/T
// with Keq in mol/cm^3 (converted internally to (kmol/m^3)^dn).
// Coefficients A1..A5 and the reaction energies are from
//     C. Park, "On convergence of computation of chemically reacting flows",
//     AIAA-85-0247 (1985), Table 1.
//
// KeqTheta = reaction energy / R, in K, from the same table:
//     O2 = 2O      117.98 kcal/mol ->  59369.9 K
//     N2 = 2N      225.00 kcal/mol -> 113224.4 K
//     NO = N + O   150.03 kcal/mol ->  75498.1 K
//     NO + O ...    32.05 kcal/mol ->  16128.2 K
//     N2 + O ...    74.97 kcal/mol ->  37726.4 K
//
// KeqTmin: the quartic fit is a high-temperature correlation and diverges
// below roughly 1500 K. Below KeqTmin the solver substitutes the correct
// asymptote ln Keq = alpha - KeqTheta/T, matched to the fit at KeqTmin.
// Verified against statistical mechanics in validate_Keq.py; the
// continuation is accurate to better than a factor of 5 down to 300 K,
// against an error of e^3754 for the raw fit at that temperature.
//
// The third body cancels out of Keq, so all five reactions of a dissociation
// family share one set of Keq inputs. Any typo therefore shows up as one
// entry disagreeing with four identical siblings.
//
// twoTemperature: MUST be true for alphaPark to have any effect. Without it
// controllingTemperature() returns TTR and the Park coupling is inert.
//
// Forward Arrhenius A, beta, Ta are unchanged from the previous mechanism.
// Units: A in m^3/(kmol s), i.e. Park's cm^3/(mol s) divided by 1000.
//
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

